## Context
Child of tracker 1317 (forge leaks). Skill prose that prescribes raw `gh` commands, today
fenced with `<!-- harness-extension-point -->` markers. The recipe is executed by
`scripts/raid_land.py` through forge.py; the prose should name the same forge.py commands so
a reader on a no-forge repository or another forge follows a working path.

Sites on main 2026-10-28:
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` (~101-216: comment, view, ready, auto-merge read and disarm, merge,
  read-back, queued-merge wait)
- `skills/merge/references/claims.md` (~18: body edit and read-back)
- `skills/lair/SKILL.md` (~71: auto-merge setting read and arm)
- `skills/roar/runbooks/capture.md` (~82: PR body read hint)

Needs the forge.py CLI from 1318. `rules/git.md`'s example (`gh pr edit … && gh pr view`)
documents forge mechanics concretely by design (scripts/check-agnostic.sh note); leave it.

Parent: tracker 1317.

## Plan (raid f7fa41: Imagine, Blind-Spot, feasibility PASS)
- Name `raid_land.py` and 1318's `forge.py` subcommands (`list`, `files`, `read-back`); the
  queued-merge wait (merge/SKILL.md ~215) becomes a `forge.py read-back` loop. Do not invent a
  `forge.py merge` CLI; a step with no forge.py spelling keeps its marker, reason in the log.
- lair/SKILL.md ~71 (repository auto-merge setting): no verb, keep behind its marker.
- First test: every `forge.py <sub>` named in the four files answers `--help` with exit 0
  (catches prose naming a subcommand that does not exist, which check-agnostic cannot).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The four files above name forge.py commands where a forge.py verb exists, and keep a
      `gh` spelling only behind an extension-point marker with a reason in this ticket's log
- [ ] Every forge.py command the prose names exists and is exercised by a test
- [ ] `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes
- [ ] `make check` passes
